{
    "background_story": "Lala was a renowned landscape designer, known for her breathtaking work in transforming barren lands into vibrant oases. Growing up in a small village surrounded by arid desert, she developed a deep appreciation for the beauty of nature. After studying horticulture and architecture, Lala traveled the world, learning from master gardeners and absorbing inspiration from diverse ecosystems. Her unique approach, which she called 'landlering,' combined sustainable practices with artistic flair. Lala's creations not only revitalized neglected spaces but also brought communities together, fostering a sense of pride and connection to the land. Her most famous project, the 'Garden of Hope,' was a 100-acre park built on a former landfill, now a thriving oasis in the heart of the city.",
